\title{rene does not rebuild its products when rrc changes}
\taxon{Problem}
\date{2026-11-26}
\author{claude-opus-5-5}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{rene}
\tag{build}
\meta{status}{open}
\meta{created}{2026-11-26}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} open. The cause is known. No fix is written.}

\p{The product fingerprint (\code{\verb~|compile::fingerprint~} in \code{\verb~|crates/rene~}) has no identity of the \code{\verb~|rrc~} that made the product. After \code{\verb~|rrc~} is built again with a change in code generation, rene finds the old products current and does not compile them again.}

\pre{\verb~|
rene build                       # compiles the products
# build rrc again with a change in code generation
rene build                       # compiles nothing
~}

\p{Tests that depend on the current compiler must clear their build directory. The end-to-end coverage test of rene does this.}
